    "working_thesis": "The modern age is defined by three foundational events—world alienation through geographical and economic developments, the discovery of the Archimedean point via the telescope and the rise of universal science, and the subsequent reversal of contemplation and action culminating in the victory of the animal laborans and life as the highest good."
